{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>He saw the first portion for himself.</b> The meaning: he saw for himself and sought a portion for himself before Israel." "<b>For there a portion is.</b> Like חֵלֶק (portion)." "And <b>a lawgiver</b> is the great one and the ruler, like לְבִי לְחֹקְקֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (my heart is with the lawgivers of Israel)." "And <b>sealed</b> is like וְסָפֻן בָּאֶרֶז (sealed with cedar). Its meaning is that they are סְפוּנִים (paneled/ceilinged), and likewise קִירוֹת הַסָּפוֹן. The meaning is that he saw paneled palaces that were the portion of the great ones of the Amorite." "<b>And he came.</b> Defective of alef. The meaning is that the heads of Gad came with Israel, armed for battle, and Moses saw this in prophecy." "<b>The righteousness of YHWH he performed.</b> That he fulfilled with his hand what He spoke through his mouth, which the children of Gad vowed — to go out with Israel to fight against their enemies. And he did not mention Reuben. It is possible that this is because the children of Gad were mightier than the children of Reuben. And behold, the words of Chronicles are eternal witness, for it says of the children of Gad וּפְנֵי אַרְיֵה פְּנֵיהֶם (and their faces were like the face of a lion), and you will not find likewise of the children of Reuben."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {3 "The parenthetical reading '(בתוכם ספונים) [צ״ל בבתיכ׳ ספוני׳]' appears to be a scribal or editorial marginal note suggesting a correction 'read: in their houses, paneled'; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:41.768976218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}